{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y9ahSmCe1Vce9gb4yRGRh2","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now let me generate the comprehensive report. Based on my thorough exploration of the three crates, I can now provide a complete verification report:\n\n## COMPREHENSIVE VERIFICATION REPORT\n\n### 1. TUI SCREENS - VERIFIED\n\n**Files examined:**\n- `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_tui/src/screens/overview.rs`\n- `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_tui/src/screens/chemistry.rs`\n- `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_tui/src/screens/biology.rs`\n- `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_tui/src/screens/actions.rs`\n- `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_tui/src/screens/log.rs`\n- `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_tui/src/screens/mod.rs`\n\nAll five required screens are implemented:\n\n**Overview Screen** (lines 1-131 in overview.rs):\n- Day/hour display (line 22)\n- Water temperature + ambient temperature (lines 23-26)\n- pH, DO/saturation (lines 27-29)\n- TAN and NH3 (lines 31-33)\n- Nitrite and nitrate (lines 35-37)\n- Hardware section: Volume, DIC, GH, KH, TDS, light intensity and photoperiod, heater status, aeration (lines 43-67)\n- Plant status: Fast stem biomass/health, rosette biomass/health (lines 69-84)\n- Shrimp status: Adults/juveniles/berried, condition, molt stress, reproductive readiness (lines 86-105)\n- Active warnings section (lines 107-121)\n\n**Chemistry Screen** (lines 1-147 in chemistry.rs):\n- Dissolved chemistry: pH, TAN, NH3, nitrite, nitrate, phosphate, DIC (lines 21-38)\n- Derived display values: DO, GH, KH, TDS, conductivity, temperature (lines 40-59)\n- Recent trends: pH trend (line 61-68), TAN trend (line 69-76), DO trend (line 77-84), temperature trend (line 85-92)\n- Sparkline visualizations for each trend\n\n**Biology Screen** (lines 1-125 in biology.rs):\n- Plant guilds: Fast stem and root rosette with biomass/health, substrate nutrients (lines 21-37)\n- Algae and detritus: Suspended algae, periphyton, nuisance index, detritus metrics (lines 39-59)\n- Shrimp population: Adults/juveniles/berried, condition, molt stress, reproductive readiness (lines 61-80)\n- Biofilter maturity: Maturity index, AOB, NOB, comammox, decomposer biomass (lines 82-94)\n- Microfauna summary: Population index, grazing pressure, filter cleanliness, aeration status (lines 96-124)\n\n**Actions Screen** (lines 1-469 in actions.rs):\nComplete action system with 12 action types implemented:\n- Feed (grams input)\n- Water change percent with source water selection\n- Trim plants (fraction)\n- Siphon detritus (fraction)\n- Clean filter (intensity)\n- Add shrimp (count)\n- Remove shrimp (count)\n- Change photoperiod (hours)\n- Change light intensity (intensity index)\n- Change heater setpoint (C)\n- Change ambient temperature (C)\n- Change aeration (toggle enabled + intensity)\n\nAll actions validate input and dispatch to PlayerAction enum (lines 308-354)\n\n**Log Screen** (lines 1-49 in log.rs):\n- Chronological event list with severity levels (Info/Warning/Critical)\n- Event metadata: Day, hour, kind, summary, cause codes\n- Color-coded display by severity\n\n---\n\n### 2. TUI CONTROLS - VERIFIED\n\n**File:** `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_tui/src/input.rs`\n\nAll required controls are implemented:\n\n- **Step 1 hour:** `h` key (line 20)\n- **Step 1 day:** `d` key (line 21)\n- **Step 1 week:** `w` key (line 22) - steps 24*7=168 hours\n- **Pause/Autoadvance:** `space` key (line 19) - toggles `auto_advance` flag\n- **Save to disk:** `s` key (lines 23-27)\n- **Load from disk:** `l` key (lines 28-32)\n- **Quit:** `q` key (line 17)\n- **Screen navigation:** Tab cycles screens (line 18), number keys 1-5 jump to specific screens (lines 33-37)\n- **Actions screen input:** Up/Down for action selection, Left/Right for field selection, bracket keys for cycling choices, `t` for toggles, digit/dot input for numeric fields, Backspace for deletion, Enter to submit\n\n---\n\n### 3. TUI