es\n- History is maintained automatically\n\n**Stepping pattern** (lines 196-211 in lib.rs):\n```rust\npub fn step_hours(&mut self, hours: u32) {\n    match self.engine.step_hours(hours) {\n        Ok(()) => {\n            self.refresh_snapshot();\n            // Status message...\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n- Time advances through `engine.step_hours()`, not direct mutation\n- Snapshot refreshed immediately after\n\nThis confirms the TUI correctly uses the snapshot-based, action-dispatch architecture without direct state mutation.\n\n---\n\n### 4. DATA PRESETS (TOML) - VERIFIED\n\n**All data files found in:** `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_data/data/`\n\n**Source Water Presets** (4 required):\n1. `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_data/data/source_water/soft_acidic.toml` ✓\n   - id, name, temperature_c, ammonia/nitrite/nitrate/phosphate, dic/doc/don\n   - Alkalinity, calcium, magnesium, sodium, potassium, bicarbonate, chloride, sulfate\n   - Provenance block with source_title, source_year, confidence, notes\n\n2. `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_data/data/source_water/moderate.toml` ✓\n3. `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_data/data/source_water/hard_shrimp.toml` ✓\n4. `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_data/data/source_water/ro_like.toml` ✓\n\n**Substrate Presets** (4 required):\n1. `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_data/data/substrate/inert_sand.toml` ✓\n2. `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_data/data/substrate/inert_gravel.toml` ✓\n3. `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_data/data/substrate/active_planted.toml` ✓\n4. `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_data/data/substrate/coarse_porous.toml` ✓\n\nEach has: id, name, depth_cm, cation_exchange_capacity_index, detritus_trapping_index, colonizable_area_factor, low_oxygen_tendency_index, grazing_surface_index, nutrient_charge_mg_n_total, nutrient_charge_mg_p_total, provenance block\n\n**Plant Presets** (2 required):\n1. `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_data/data/plants/fast_stem.toml` ✓\n2. `/root/tank-simulation